CoWPositionExecutor
├── constructor
│   └── zero owner, adapter and lender: accept; initialize router-derived dependencies
├── events
│   ├── Arm: publish the exact intent, order hash and UID
│   └── FlashLoanAndCallBack: publish completed principal and premium in both directions
├── gas snapshots
│   └── isolated non-fuzz metering covers all exposed functions and both callback directions
├── order hashing
│   ├── vendored GPv2Order hash matches independent canonical EIP-712 encoding for every field
│   ├── hashing preserves the order, preceding memory word and free-memory pointer
│   ├── executor order hash and derived UID match canonical encoding across directions and order parameters
│   └── initial UID is empty and the zero hash has no valid signature
├── arm
│   ├── unauthorized, live intent or zero output/input: reject
│   ├── any nonzero uint96 native value, including the high bit: reject
│   ├── expired intent: replace and revoke previous sell-token approval and signature
│   ├── last completed order: remain inactive with no allowance; fresh order can replace immediately
│   ├── identical tokens or malformed action parameters: defer failure to execution
│   └── valid intent: bind exact order, calls and bounded relayer allowance
├── isValidSignature
│   ├── inactive, wrong digest or expired: reject
│   └── armed order: validate independently of signature bytes, current root or flash execution context
├── execute
│   ├── owner rearming or router requesting a second loan while busy: rollback
│   ├── unauthenticated router/lender, wrong initiator or modified callback data: reject
│   ├── third-party flash loan: trusted Aave supplies the third-party initiator and the executor rejects
│   ├── arbitrary router lender/token/amount metadata cannot alter the committed loan or position effects
│   ├── leverage: swap, supply and borrow through current Merkle roles
│   ├── deleverage: repay and withdraw through current Merkle roles, then swap
│   ├── missing/stale fill, replayed order, low output, premium excess or repayment shortfall: rollback
│   ├── malformed action/proof/role or capability health query: fail closed and rollback
│   ├── capability health below its current floor or adapter idle balance loss: rollback
│   ├── changed root: current adapter proofs still gate execution; authorized actions may change the root
│   └── success: consume intent, clear allowances and return surplus/donations to adapter
└── expiry
    ├── permit execution through validTo, then revoke signature and execution authorization
    └── next arm may select different sell token and clears the expired order allowance

Stateful arm/execute/expire-and-rearm/completed-rearm sequences
└── preserve idle strategy funds and health, no residual flash custody, exact active allowance
